    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Since, as stated by the quoted theorems, any real section GR of a complex g is isomorphic to Gθ for a suitable θ, it follows that the splitting of the Cartan subalgebra of any GR, into a compact and non-compact subalgebra has an intrinsic meaning. Hence for every real section GR we can define the compact and non-compact rank as follows:"
